No absolute speedup is assumed.","300-color input exercises Wu plus its measured error accounting; it is not a real photograph/video workload. Compact-size baselines reproduce the prior 256-entry local table and minimum LZW code size 8; both outputs are independently decoded through WIC.","Temporal reuse never approximates <=255-color UI input. For higher-color inputs, every accepted reused RGB channel is checked against a maximum error of 8 levels. Static synthetic-gradient indices are checked unchanged. No dithering is implemented; real photograph/video subjective flicker and banding acceptance requires inspecting the optional quality artifacts.","real_0 input=frame-0000.png","real_1 input=frame-0001.png","real_2 input=frame-0002.png","real_3 input=frame-0003.png","real_4 input=frame-0004.png","real_5 input=frame-0005.png","real_6 input=frame-0006.png","real_7 input=frame-0007.png","real_8 input=frame-0008.png","real_9 input=frame-0009.png","real_10 input=frame-0010.png","real_11 input=frame-0011.png","Real inputs are decoded by Windows WIC, aspect-preserving Fant-scaled only when exceeding 1920x1080. Metrics compare decoded 8-bit RGB code values, without ICC conversion, EXIF orientation handling, linear-light conversion or dithering. Source decoding, GIF encoding and error measurement are excluded from quantization timings.","Per-file GIFs and ordered-input GIFs are saved for visual review. Ordered inputs are filename-sorted; equal-size contiguous groups play at 10fps solely for comparison, not the original video timing. Input provenance determines whether a sequence is real video; arbitrary photographs are not labelled video. PSNR is omitted for lossless RGB (mathematically infinite). Numeric success does not certify subjective banding/flicker quality."]}
